  "strict_win_record_note": "Cross-round ratios carry fresh-fixture variation at least as large as the differences between the recent rounds, so the record is not a precise ranking. The round-0014 winner source, unchanged and with an identical source-manifest hash, measured winner/rho 0.7818 instructions and 0.9424 native in round-0014 and 0.7372 and 0.9246 in round-0015 -- the same executable, different fixtures. Round-0013 holds the record on the native metric (0.9098) and round-0015 shows the lowest instruction ratio (0.7372); neither dominates, and the record is left where it was rather than moved on a difference this measurement cannot separate from fixture draw. Round 0016 widened the panel to eight cells and beats_rho_strict came back FALSE: the winner loses to rho outright at n23a1 (instructions 1.0656) and at n29a1 (native 1.0905), and the panel-wide native upper limit is 1.0288. The same receipts restricted to the legacy five cells still pass strictly (native 0.9341, upper 0.9653, every cell below one), so every strict-win record above -- round 0013 included -- is scoped to that five-cell panel and must not be restated at family level. The record pointer is left at round-0013 because it names the best five-cell measurement, not because the claim survives a wider panel.",
